{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:7e42a3bddefbedc3048f1f76191b62e7ee0c5e7328b45f30a5bf5be9581b836b","title":"The mobile D3 position provides the inflaton candidate in a warped throat. Warping suppresses the anti-D3 energy, while conifold geometry supplies calculable radial and angular dependence for forces induced by moduli stabilization.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e520fbaf61d77030aa0418f33394a76e1cf03d378677327f2f6dd3f1c19fbac","title":"How should a finite-temperature effective action be defined for nonadiabatically driven QED with pair creation, and how do initial thermal populations affect vacuum polarization and the imaginary action?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0009"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e7e59123cf54f929916f12eb059964fa7f512d7038a493f730b81f187a00e98","title":"Do the nonsupersymmetric AdS local minima admit a nonperturbative decay compatible with the conjecture excluding stable nonsupersymmetric AdS vacua?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e9bf861891adc9f8fc5beb04a30c207b40d394c66cf665385a9e9c28431c11d","title":"How do torus geometry and brane distributions control the spectrum and vacuum energy in D-dimensional orientifolds with a single Scherk–Schwarz direction? Corner backgrounds reduce the brane data to integer multiplicities paired across that direction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ecf2fe1cb767200abb93cc1b89d356b4825329b44542d8b501805775519e179","title":"Can a non-geometric holographic early universe address the smoothness/horizon, flatness, and relic problems through properties of the dual QFT's RG flow, and offer an account of the arrow of time?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e28f97f4919c8cca2e83ba702925351b1b3764ce2cf509c344dbac720ed8861","title":"What quantum uncertainty applies to the scalar assigned to an entire Hubble patch? Appendix C treats that scalar as a normalized spatial average on a Cauchy surface, with RMS field displacement and RMS velocity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7eb4984f515ae331a2797a4edb2d442d9876753ed79394a7f4504991e96f227b","title":"Can FRW boundary correlators define a quantum theory encompassing multiple dS parents and landscape transitions? The source identifies unknown perturbation boundary conditions, a missing Hilbert-space interpretation, and an unestablished averaging prescription.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e76495a7292e07fa3cdd3f5ee24317c445f091ffb3fa97c5b055387ca463dfb","title":"How do extremal black holes and light towers behave near infinite distance with several scalar and gauge fields? The principal setting is four-dimensional N=2 Type IIB compactification on a Calabi–Yau threefold.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e3e2b833243bd3ee73678c8222201109bc3f703f6a97f395471d784bbd0450d","title":"Do supersymmetric recombined branes exist for an unbounded sequence of negative D3 charges? The paper proposes their nonperturbative stability as a test of finite-vacua conjectures, conditional on completing the configurations into distinct vacua satisfying the conjecture's fixed bounds.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e9e95b146062e6d0a496a51dc7767b2bf7054e472d8e99b95096cb1693741de","title":"How strongly do Euclidean gravitational wormholes break continuous global symmetries, and do their actions preserve Peccei–Quinn axion quality? The paper also asks how an extended global symmetry and an open-string axion–dilaton system change the answer when radial modes are dynamical.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e27a7f1b03a9b3ddef19dbc12d9c743a715e85d8b04d39f6be8742b6ae00ae6","title":"Can additional AdS decay destinations make uplifted string-theoretic dS vacua short-lived enough to satisfy the assumed TCC bound, and are the underlying static four-dimensional assumptions compatible with higher-dimensional equations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ef23ff3780e1adc0208dda55b8ae62d1f104007f14001b65783f2a81173bc3f","title":"Which discrete 2-form symmetries of 6D (2,0) and (1,0) SCFT sectors survive screening when coupled to gravity, and how does the embedding of string-charge lattices determine their gauging?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e21429df31d5a6ea27fb6e6854659b14864494e66fe6f80fa6cedfc4132105d","title":"Does asymptotic mass growth as a gauge coupling tends to zero constrain BPS decays throughout the perturbative region, and what does this imply for the stability and population of light charged towers?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ea7f38f3938ca2c54a9cf97b3a14334f0bb1a575cd25ab04749b960b347f9d1","title":"Which massless U(1) charge spectra occur in F-theory compactifications, beyond satisfying known low-energy consistency conditions? The paper seeks a geometric diagnostic that could help distinguish realizable spectra from an infinite set of candidate six-dimensional spectra.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7eab9a098f85c6a0b7562d4142c361bcaf441b882f40d53761b48e1cb315dc17","title":"Can a smoother metric formulation determine the interior, entropy and gravitational-wave travel time of arbitrarily large thermal 2-2-holes, and clarify their implications for black-hole-based WGC arguments?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e29dc4ab74f40cb4e54f98b2eccaa2997a4a03aad753f0e6bf8ff653d08840a","title":"A nonminimally coupled composite NJL scalar is used to generate a plateau inflationary potential.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ea95248d5ad057316e28935410e3b9fbc58f6d7ba3f9a4d01310f33e9c48344","title":"Can inflationary Schwinger production alone generate the observed dark matter abundance, including light charged particles whose purely gravitational production is negligible, in a secluded dark sector that never thermalizes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0086"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ebdc1935c62f82d51f6ef1d618b4ca6c32917e1b49daf97a336fa18f191409c","title":"How does allowing axions to move alongside runaway saxions change the late-time Hubble slow-roll parameter and the stability of its constant-value solutions, especially for the Type IIB volume modulus and axio-dilaton?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0087"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7eb208016529ba18569ed761fc17877569297d5fee9995048b8865d0788eb7fd","title":"Can the inflationary e-folding restriction be expressed as an information bound using stochastic inflaton entropy, and can volume weighting supply entropy behavior that respects the de Sitter horizon bound during eternal inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0088"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e20c59adca55cf6639957178a7dd3dbffae7c89a6a6d00555102da06a1478b0","title":"How many light axions can be produced through independent Standard Model interactions, and how do operator dimension, flavor structure and reheating determine their contribution to ΔNeff and CMB discovery prospects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0097"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e28d7de9d8736205eb58bf65cf185aa24d701b01607c0ce60c88758c25b4954","title":"How do approximate axionic shift symmetries and gradients of BPS string tensions and particle masses characterise gravity decoupling, kinetic mixing and curvature divergences in asymptotic moduli-space limits?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0100"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ef040afb8643c699191e0f5fcb788413d8b6d52eec8676289a07d9ec012b979","title":"Can the mirror description of complex-structure moduli through complexified Kähler structures supply natural semi-toric partial compactifications, including a minimal analogue of Satake–Baily–Borel and boundary descriptions beyond normal crossings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0103"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ebc51e5198ec3aeeefa5f45c261821b80198a81057463793194b8a1e6d3e133","title":"Can rapid nonperturbative transfer of modulus energy into Standard Model bosons, through tachyonic resonance, suppress subsequent direct gravitino production, and what approximate modulus-mass range permits this mechanism?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0106"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ee28f87899cceb297cbe7435d0e7fda91ab7e8853f3d7b83b4b56a8f31031b4","title":"What economical gauged nonabelian family symmetry can distinguish the heavy third family and organize lighter masses while satisfying anomaly cancellation and adding no new quarks?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0106"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7ec23ab966a35e14743e982acc13567ac54b7c493d850c575801004d2ecad796","title":"Does the proposed first-order deformation of 10D, N=1 superspace yield bosonic equations admitting compatible component actions in both two-form and six-form formulations, and equivalence to the gravitational part of the existing anomaly-free component action?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0112"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e582c2c762e8d943d534c250584185a3e2a4016e9e4cc2126be8b57798600ea","title":"Can warping and world-volume fluxes support open-string tachyon inflation within KKLT-inspired moduli stabilization, satisfying e-fold and perturbation requirements while admitting initial conditions motivated by open-string completeness?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0113"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e4d0fa11989168438522ee37fe7a6d72b7d81c9f2e3db96da0b1394556de78d","title":"Which four-dimensional N=2 heterotic compactifications admit type II Calabi–Yau duals, allowing exact quantum moduli geometry to be inferred from the other description, and how can apparently different heterotic vacua be connected?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0118"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e729461165f25b5599b2b2b461a6d4707b7065208572ce3fb1c9381fd787728","title":"Can uncompactified eleven-dimensional M-theory in the infinite-momentum frame be defined exactly by the large-N limit of D0-brane matrix quantum mechanics, reproducing supergravitons, their interactions, membranes and the required spacetime symmetries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0119"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e5175d777662401d50ebcfea1b911a0534d72873f48347eebf87e2804a8ac94","title":"How can six-dimensional (1,0) supergravity be coupled simultaneously to arbitrary numbers of tensor, vector and hypermultiplets, including gauging, and what singularities and anomaly constraints accompany these couplings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0119"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e3a11bcffc26d2fda99db1f177f9aabc362fb83c39e655be9e907acb432c809","title":"Can Born–Infeld theory on a noncommutative two-torus describe compactified D-brane dynamics with T-duality acting on fluctuations as well as global charges, and how can its extra parameter θ be related to the string B-field modulus?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0120"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:7e5b2e05b2df3f2fb0c384347f97d834dd15da377cbee60203fdc21a4ff80ccf","title":"How can boundary SYM encode distant bulk collisions before their signals reach the boundary, while its stress tensor subsequently exhibits apparently instantaneous redistribution, superluminal oscillations and negative local energy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:439a4b7a2bceda86ac6fa5de","source":"q025-candidate-question:ad46b9d192cc6d5b336bffb2","target":"source-question:7e42a3bddefbedc3048f1f76191b62e7ee0c5e7328b45f30a5bf5be9581b836b","detail":{"shardId":"relation-details-0039","recordSha256":"d35e02fecb93485f0bc222e4e206cb0013d68fe26190c5be330b4b23a8a4a9e0"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-access:8d0e4b65aa5e6544232d0405","source":"q025-placement-question:65ae00d173332a6d969acd0c","target":"source-question:7e520fbaf61d77030aa0418f33394a76e1cf03d378677327f2f6dd3f1c19fbac"